From dccbdbadb2fd9f571fb854a37a32123008987a6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vlad Zahorodnii <vlad.zahorodnii@kde.org>
Date: Fri, 5 Jul 2024 13:29:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] plugins/screenshot: Drop X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces

The security benefits of the current approach are doubtful. The desktop
files can be modified or overriden by the user, which makes the
X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces checks pointless. The best available
option at the moment are sandbox environments like flatpak.

(cherry picked from commit 0ea31ae72eb052cb9c9cc508318fc3f0f329ed53)

Backported to Stereo KWin 6.7.4: the workspace capture's description in
org.kde.KWin.ScreenShot2.xml keeps its sentences about stereo outputs,
and the screenshot_test_support library of our autotests stops linking
KF6::Service too, like the plugin, since no file of it uses KService
any more. The rest is as upstream wrote it. f9bf0ee6 and 97b5274a, the
same merge request's changes to the restricted Wayland interfaces, are
not part of this.

Origin: backport, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/commit/0ea31ae72eb052cb9c9cc508318fc3f0f329ed53
Author: Vlad Zahorodnii <vlad.zahorodnii@kde.org>
Applied-Upstream: v6.8.0, 0ea31ae7 (merge request !6057)
Last-Update: 2026-11-01

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
